    stdlib [38;5;153mcsv[39m module with [38;5;153mlineterminator="\n"[39m so the file doesn't pick up CRLF.
  - [38;5;153mrender_json(rows, day) -> str[39m — [38;5;153m{"day": "2026-09-11", "accounts": [{"account_id": "acct-1", "cents": 1050}, ...], [39m
    [38;5;153m"total_cents": 1325}[39m, [38;5;153mindent=2[39m. The [38;5;153mday[39m field makes the file self-describing once it's detached from the filename;
    [38;5;153mtotal_cents[39m is the cross-check against the emailed total.

  Row order is whatever [38;5;153mdaily_rows()[39m returns, which is already [38;5;153mORDER BY account_id[39m. Both are pure string-returning
  functions like [38;5;153mrender_text()[39m — the file write stays in the CLI layer.

  [1mBehavior decisions I'm making unless you say otherwise:[0m
  - Overwrites an existing file silently. Cron jobs get re-run after failures, and a re-run of the same day should be
    idempotent, not an error.
  - A missing parent directory fails with a clear [38;5;153mClickException[39m, not a traceback — cron mails stderr to
    [38;5;153mbilling-ops@example.com[39m, and a stack trace is a bad thing to page ops with.
  - A day with no rows is a valid export, not an error: CSV is the header alone, JSON has [38;5;153m"accounts": [][39m and
    [38;5;153m"total_cents": 0[39m.
  - Trailing newline at end of file in both formats.

  [1mFiles touched:[0m [38;5;153mcli.py[39m, [38;5;153msummarize.py[39m, tests, and one line in the README's CLI list. No new dependencies — [38;5;153mcsv[39m and [38;5;153mjson[39m
  are stdlib. No version bump unless you ask.

  [1mTesting:[0m renderer tests go in [38;5;153mtests/test_summarize.py[39m following the existing pure-function pattern (round-trip the CSV
  through [38;5;153mcsv.reader[39m, the JSON through [38;5;153mjson.loads[39m, assert cents stay integers, cover the empty-rows case). I'd add one
  new [38;5;153mtests/test_export_cli.py[39m using click's [38;5;153mCliRunner[39m with [38;5;153mreportkit.cli.connect[39m/[38;5;153mdaily_rows[39m monkeypatched, writing to
  [38;5;153mtmp_path[39m — the file-write path is the actual new risk and there's no DB in the test environment. That's the one place
  I'd extend beyond the current testing pattern; say the word if you'd rather keep tests to the pure renderers only.
  TDD: tests first.

  [1mOne thing I can't do from here:[0m [38;5;153mdeploy/crontab[39m calls [38;5;153m/usr/local/bin/reportkit-nightly[39m, which isn't in this repo. To
  actually produce nightly files, that wrapper needs two added [38;5;153mexport[39m calls (one per format) alongside the existing
  [38;5;153msummarize[39m. I can add a comment to [38;5;153mdeploy/crontab[39m recording that if you want, but I'd rather not touch the deploy file
